   "adjustments": [],
   "text": "Here is the uncomfortable truth. Most creators price from fear, not from value. They pick the number that feels safe to say out loud. When I started, I charged $200 for a launch video that made my client $40,000 in a week. The video was not the problem. My price was nobody pays you for your hours. They pay you for the result. So that is the trap with hourly rates. Exactly. An hourly rate punishes you for getting faster. The better you get, the less you earn. What do you tell people to do instead? I use a simple three -number test before every proposal. Right down your floor, the price where you would walk away. Then your target, the price that is fair for the result."
  },
